            <ArticleTitle>Neuropathic pain and dry eye.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1542-0124(17)30068-X</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jtos.2017.10.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dry eye is a common, multifactorial disease currently diagnosed by a combination of symptoms and signs. Its epidemiology and clinical presentation have many similarities with neuropathic pain outside the eye. This review highlights the similarities between dry eye and neuropathic pain, focusing on clinical features, somatosensory function, and underlying pathophysiology. Implications of these similarities on the diagnosis and treatment of dry eye are discussed.</AbstractText>
